  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Lead lost in the eleventh when the defense had no margin left.",
    "what_this_means": "Robbie Ray delivered six scoreless innings. The offense built a two-run lead in the fourth and held it through eight. A rare window of control in a season defined by inconsistency. Then the ninth inning arrived. Two runs crossed before the Padres could answer, and the tie held through ten scoreless frames. In the eleventh, with nothing left to give, Mason Miller and David Morgan allowed two more. France's sac fly had given Tampa Bay the go-ahead. Twelve strikeouts and one conversion on nine RISP opportunities. The math was always going to matter here. This is what happens when the margin between winning and losing shrinks to one run: the next mistake decides it, and there's no time to recover.",
    "what_to_watch": "Brady Singer has posted a 4.72 ERA this season, and the Padres need Michael King's recent form. A 2.14 ERA over his last four starts. To hold up tonight in Cincinnati.",
